WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.990
It was Chancellor Angela Merkel's first parliamentary
speech since announcing she would step down

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:06.490
as party leader.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.470
And she was unusually passionate.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:14.040
She vigorously defended the UN migration pact,
saying acting internationally was the only

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.190
way to solve global problems.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:24.130
It's in our national interest to improve the
conditions for refugees on the one hand, and

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.640
for employment migration on the other.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.790
This was a budget debate - traditionally a
chance for the opposition to attack the government's

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:34.930
policies.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:40.090
But the largest opposition party, the far-right
AfD, is under pressure itself.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:48.150
Stung by a scandal over campaign donations,
the AfD parliamentary co-leader lashed out.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:55.730
You have no right to criticise us on moral
grounds!

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:59.000
Step out of your glass house and stop throwing
stones.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.780
You'll only hit yourself in the end !

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:10.460
The 
nice thing about free debates is that everyone

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:15.359
can talk about whatever they think is important
for the country.

00:01:15.359 --> 00:01:23.749
Smaller opposition parties took the government
to task for quarrelling and inaction.

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:25.340
People are sick of the coalition.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:30.670
With its bad compromises and impasses, it's
clearly incapable of solving people's real

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:33.450
problems.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:38.479
This coalition is like a self-help group that's
concerned only with itself and not with the

00:01:38.479 --> 00:01:43.149
needs of society.

00:01:43.149 --> 00:01:48.450
After such unusually animated parliamentary
exchanges, politicians returned to the rather

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.499
drier task of discussing next year's budget.

